# Minotaur

## Lore

The Minotaur is the bull-headed monster of Greek myth: a black-skinned giant with the head of a bull and the body of a muscular humanoid. Minotaurs are thought to have crossed the Megaverse first as henchmen and enforcers of the Old Ones, then as refugees through dimensional portals; Space Minotaurs live in the Three Galaxies. They were wiped from the Earth before recorded history, but with the return of magic they are found there again - as adventurers, explorers, mercenaries or refugees, alone, in pairs or in small bands. They were probably wandering vegetarians once, and still prefer grain, fruit and vegetables to meat.

On the Palladium World great fields of Minotaur bones lie in the Baalgor Wastelands, the mark of a campaign to exterminate them whose authors even the Minotaurs do not know. The survivors took to underground complexes full of traps and pits. On Rifts Earth they are uncommon, known mainly as slave stock and arena fighters on Atlantis, and are mistaken for mutant animals, D-Bees or demon Bulls.

**Alignment:** Evil or Selfish.

**Height:** 8 to 11 feet (2.4 to 3.3 m). **Weight:** 500 to 800 pounds (225 to 360 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 400 years.

## GM Notes

Palladium Minotaurs are wary of all humanoids and live in shame and seclusion for having once served the Old Ones, but the rare adventurer tolerates most races and may befriend any. They love large swords and axes, and those who know modern weapons love Vibro-Blades and heavy weapons and armor. They prefer warm and temperate climates.
